# Detecting and Responding to System Theme Changes in .NET MAUI

## Get the Current Theme

```csharp
AppTheme currentTheme = Application.Current.RequestedTheme;
// Returns AppTheme.Light, AppTheme.Dark, or AppTheme.Unspecified
```

## Subscribe to Theme Change Events

```csharp
Application.Current.RequestedThemeChanged += (s, e) =>
{
    AppTheme newTheme = e.RequestedTheme;
    Debug.WriteLine($"Theme changed to: {newTheme}");
    // Update UI or trigger re-theming logic here
};
```

This fires in real time whenever the user toggles dark/light mode in device settings.

## Force a Specific Theme (Override System Setting)

```csharp
// Force dark mode
Application.Current.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Dark;

// Force light mode
Application.Current.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Light;

// Revert to following the system setting
Application.Current.UserAppTheme = AppTheme.Unspecified;
```

Setting `UserAppTheme` overrides the system theme. The `RequestedThemeChanged` event still fires when the system theme changes, but the app's visuals stay pinned to your chosen theme until you reset it to `AppTheme.Unspecified`.

## Full Example (in App.xaml.cs)

```csharp
public partial class App : Application
{
    public App()
    {
        InitializeComponent();

        RequestedThemeChanged += OnThemeChanged;
    }

    private void OnThemeChanged(object sender, AppThemeChangedEventArgs e)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"System theme is now: {e.RequestedTheme}");
        // Respond: swap resources, notify ViewModels, etc.
    }

    public void SetUserThemePreference(AppTheme theme)
    {
        UserAppTheme = theme; // Dark, Light, or Unspecified
    }
}
```

## XAML: Reactive Theme Resources

You can also define theme-aware resources declaratively:

```xml
<Color x:Key="PageBackground">
    <Color.Light>White</Color.Light>
    <Color.Dark>#1C1C1E</Color.Dark>
</Color>
```

Or use `AppThemeBinding`:

```xml
<Label TextColor="{AppThemeBinding Light=Black, Dark=White}" />
```

These update automatically when the effective theme changes (whether from system or `UserAppTheme`).
